{#
    What a player has bought, and what is still waiting (FR-090, FR-095).

    This is the screen FR-095's acceptance criterion is about: "the child sees the status change
    from Pending to Confirmed". The status is a word, always — `ApprovalStatus::label()` — with an
    explanation under it, because "Expired" on its own tells a fourteen-year-old nothing about what
    happened or what to do next.

    A parent reaching this page sees their whole family's, since they are the account that answers
    for it; the list is scoped server-side to the profiles the viewer is or manages, never to an
    id in the URL.

    Until Epic-02 exists there is nothing to buy, so the "start a purchase" links go to the
    stand-in checkout and the page says as much.
#}
{% extends 'player/_layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}My reservations{% endblock %}
{% block heading %}My reservations{% endblock %}

{% block player_content %}
    {% if requests is empty %}
        <p class="muted">Nothing here yet.</p>
    {% else %}
        {% for purchase in requests %}
            <article class="purchase-card status-{{ purchase.status.value }}" aria-labelledby="reservation-{{ purchase.id }}">
                <div class="headline">
                    <h2 id="reservation-{{ purchase.id }}">{{ purchase.purchaseDescription }}</h2>
                    {{ include('approval/_amount.html.twig', {amount: purchase.amount}) }}
                </div>

                <p class="meta">
                    <span class="status status-{{ purchase.status.value }}">{{ purchase.status.label }}</span>
                    <span>{{ purchase.childProfile.displayName }}</span>
                    <span>Paid with {{ purchase.paymentType.label|lower }}</span>
                    <span>Asked {{ purchase.requestedAt|date('j M Y, H:i') }}</span>
                </p>

                <p>{{ purchase.status.explanation }}</p>

                {% if purchase.status.isPending %}
                    {{ include('approval/_countdown.html.twig', {expiresAt: purchase.expiresAt}) }}
                {% endif %}

                {% if purchase.parentNotes %}
                    <p class="notes"><strong>Note from your parent:</strong> {{ purchase.parentNotes }}</p>
                {% endif %}
            </article>
        {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}

    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="buy-heading">
        <h2 id="buy-heading">Start a purchase</h2>
        <p class="muted">
            Events arrive with a later release. Until then this stand-in stands in for their
            checkout — nothing here charges anybody.
        </p>
        <ul>
            {% for profile in profiles %}
                <li>
                    <a href="{{ path('player_checkout', {id: profile.id}) }}">
                        <span aria-hidden="true">Buy something for {{ profile.displayName }}</span>
                        <span class="visually-hidden">Start a purchase for {{ profile.displayName }}</span>
                    </a>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
